## 3. Logging - Use StructuredLogger

### ❌ WRONG

```typescript
console.log(`[${requestId}] Processing...`);
console.error('Error:', error);
console.log('DEBUG:', variable);
```

### ✅ CORRECT

```typescript
import { createLogger, performanceTimer } from '../utils/logger';

const logger = createLogger(request);
logger.info('processing_started', { requestId, operation: 'handler' });
logger.error('processing_failed', { requestId, errorCode }, error);
logger.debug('variable_state', { variable, otherData });

// Performance timing
const timer = performanceTimer(logger, 'db_query');
const result = await db.query(...);
timer.end({ rows: result.length });
```

### Rule: Structured Logging Only

```typescript
// NEVER:
console.log(...)
console.error(...)

// ALWAYS:
import { createLogger } from '../utils/logger';
const logger = createLogger(request);
logger.info(...) / logger.error(...) / logger.warn(...) / logger.debug(...)
```

